--TEST--
a call through a union finds an added method only when one `extend` block adds it to every class: two blocks that each add `label` to one class of `Book|Pen` are `E1013`, and the help says to test the value with `is` — `rule:classes/an-added-member-never-changes-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Acme\Shop\Book;
use Acme\Shop\Pen;
use App\BookTools;
use App\PenTools;

autoload 'Acme\Shop' from './vendor/acme/shop/src';

extend Book as BookTools {
    public function label(): string {
        return "book";
    }
}

extend Pen as PenTools {
    public function label(): string {
        return "pen";
    }
}

final class Names
{
    public static function of(Book|Pen $item): string
    {
        return $item->label();
    }
}

echo Names::of(new Book()), "\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/src/Book.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Acme\Shop;

final class Book
{
}
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/src/Pen.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace Acme\Shop;

final class Pen
{
}
--FILE vendor/acme/shop/package.toml--
[package]
name = 'Acme\Shop'
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E1013]: no one `extend` block adds the method `label()` to every class of `Acme\Shop\Book|Acme\Shop\Pen`
   --> %s:27:16
   |
27 |         return $item->label();
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^ called through `Acme\Shop\Book|Acme\Shop\Pen` here
   = note: `App\BookTools` adds it to `Acme\Shop\Book`, `App\PenTools` adds it to `Acme\Shop\Pen`
   = help: test the value with `is` first, and call the method on one class. A block that extends an interface every class implements adds the method to all of them

